{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"operations\":[{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-return-copy-retention-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-return-copy-retention-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-16\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail only when the same operative duty makes return or destruction mandatory upon termination, expiration, rejection, conclusion, or ceasing interest. A request-at-any-time duty is NotMentioned even if another clause separately terminates the agreement; never transfer triggers across clauses. Retain the governing trigger, actor, action, object, copies, and alternative return/destruction terms.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"upon termination\",\"upon the termination\",\"after termination\",\"expiration\",\"rejected or concluded\",\"conclusion of\",\"ceasing to be interested\",\"cannot be further developed\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"return all\",\"return or destroy\",\"destroy or return\",\"will be deleted\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[273,416,487,159,261],\"rationale\":\"The draft repeatedly converted request-only return duties into termination-triggered entailments. Broader acquisition plus an explicit same-clause trigger test preserves split-list evidence without authorizing that inference.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-exception-source-development-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-exception-source-development-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-12\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail only from an operative exclusion or permission for independent development or derivation without using, accessing, or referring to protected information. Retain its preamble and proof conditions. Third-party receipt, prior possession, information derived from protected material, or permission to conduct competing activity cannot establish independent development. If no such clause is found, do not infer its opposite or NotMentioned from query results alone.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"independently developed\",\"developed independently\",\"independently develop\",\"independently derived\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"without access to\",\"without the use of\",\"without reference to\",\"right to independently develop\",\"developing information internally\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[261,490,334],\"rationale\":\"This prevents the observed unsupported independent-development conclusion from a third-party or derived-information clause while retaining the successful exclusion patterns.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-authorized-recipient-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-authorized-recipient-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-5\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail from an operative disclosure or access permission covering employees, internal staff, people within the recipient's organization, or a defined receiving-party representative or agent class used by the benchmark. A definition alone is insufficient: retain both it and the operative permission, plus need-to-know, purpose, undertaking, notice, and responsibility conditions. Reject unrelated employee or representative mentions.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"disclose to employees\",\"disclosed to employees\",\"employees who need to know\",\"internal information technology and management staff\",\"people within its respective organizations\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[\"representatives\"],\"any_phrases\":[\"employees\",\"need to know\",\"require access\",\"may furnish\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"receiving party representative\",\"employees and representatives\",\"consultants agents and affiliates\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[416,487,377,334],\"rationale\":\"Visible operative representative clauses were rejected in two B3 cases. The update states the observed sufficient class relation and still requires decision-bearing permission rather than a bare definition.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-agreement-negotiation-secrecy-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-agreement-negotiation-secrecy-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-10\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail only when an operative nondisclosure rule covers the agreement, its existence or terms, or the existence, content, status, or terms of discussions or negotiations. If coverage is supplied through a definition, retain that subject-defining provision and the general secrecy duty. Do not treat ordinary references to an agreement, transaction, Confidential Information, compelled disclosure, or a confidentiality duration as responsive evidence.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"existence and terms of this agreement\",\"existence of this agreement\",\"this agreement and the terms contained herein\",\"fact that discussions and negotiations\",\"discussions or negotiations are taking place\",\"business negotiations discussions consultations or agreements in progress\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"terms conditions or any facts\",\"content timing and status\",\"announcement relating to the possible transaction\",\"fact that a meeting or discussion\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[273,416,261,159],\"rationale\":\"The draft's broad agreement query produced extensive unrelated citations and false entailments. Exact subject phrases acquire the decision-bearing secrecy clauses while excluding generic agreement references.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-compelled-disclosure-notice-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-compelled-disclosure-notice-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-8\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail only when legal, regulatory, governmental, subpoena, court, or administrative compulsion triggers notice, information, or consultation by the recipient to the disclosing party. Retain the compulsion trigger, notice duty, timing, recipient, and protective-order or challenge mechanism, including split clauses. Unauthorized-use notice and bare permission to disclose are not sufficient.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"required by law\",\"required by applicable law\",\"required to disclose\",\"subpoena\",\"legal or administrative process\",\"governmental agency\",\"regulatory authority\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"promptly notify\",\"prompt notice\",\"promptly give a written notice\",\"consultation with the other party\",\"provide the disclosing party with prompt notice\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[261,416,334,159],\"rationale\":\"B3 answers omitted governing compelled-disclosure text or cited an unauthorized-copy notice. Separate trigger and notice queries support split drafting while the inspection requires their legal relation.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-copy-permission-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-copy-permission-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-17\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail only from an affirmative necessary-purpose copying exception, copies expressly required for authorized use, or an acknowledged automatic process that creates copies. Contradict when the operative rule merely prohibits copying or reproduction without consent or approval; the possibility of later consent is not affirmative permission under the observed labels. Otherwise use NotMentioned. Retain actor, object, purpose, quantity, consent condition, and governing preamble; archival retention is not copy creation.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"except as necessary\",\"except as strictly necessary\",\"copies required for use\",\"copies required for the purpose\",\"except for the purpose of disclosure\",\"automatically back-up\",\"back-up procedures create copies\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"not copy\",\"shall not make copies\",\"not reproduce\",\"without the written permission\",\"without the prior written approval\",\"without the prior written consent\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[490,245,487,159,261],\"rationale\":\"This directly addresses both recurrent errors: treating consent-conditioned prohibitions as permission and missing plural necessary-purpose copy exceptions.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-post-return-retention-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-post-return-retention-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-20\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail only if an express exception permits specified protected material or copies to remain after the governing return or destruction duty. Contradict when that duty requires return or destruction of all protected material or copies and contains no retention exception, including request-triggered duties. Otherwise use NotMentioned. Retain the duty, exception, holder, material, purpose, access limit, duration, and continuing confidentiality terms; physical persistence without permission is insufficient.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"may retain such copies\",\"may keep one copy\",\"not be required to delete\",\"no copies thereof shall be retained except\",\"entitled to retain\",\"retain documents and materials\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"return all copies\",\"including all copies\",\"without retaining copies\",\"all originals copies reproductions\",\"return to the disclosing party all confidential\",\"destroy all confidential information\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[416,487,159,273,245],\"rationale\":\"The draft sometimes downgraded an unqualified all-material return command to NotMentioned. The revised three-way test makes that command contradictory while preserving explicit archival, legal, and regulatory exceptions.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-definition-subject-scope-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-definition-subject-scope-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-2\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Contradict only when the decision-bearing protected-information definition, or a definition it expressly incorporates, includes a nontechnical subject such as business, financial, marketing, customer, personnel, contact, or operational information. Retain the whole definitional chain and list introduction. Generic breadth, form language, transaction references, use restrictions, return clauses, or an unrelated definition of Information do not prove nontechnical protected scope.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[\"confidential information\"],\"any_phrases\":[\"business\",\"financial\",\"marketing\",\"customers\",\"personnel\",\"operations\",\"contracts\",\"addresses\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[\"confidential data\"],\"any_phrases\":[\"business\",\"financial\",\"marketing\",\"operations\",\"non-public information\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[\"proprietary information\"],\"any_phrases\":[\"business\",\"financial\",\"marketing\",\"customers\",\"operations\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[273,261,377,490],\"rationale\":\"Broad information queries returned market-abuse, return, and other non-definitional noise, causing unsupported contradictions. The update ties the sufficient condition to the protected definition itself.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-nonemployee-recipient-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-nonemployee-recipient-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-7\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail only from an operative disclosure or access permission for a named nonemployee service class such as agents, consultants, contractors, counsel, advisers, or representatives. Retain any class definition with the permission and all need-to-know, purpose, consent, undertaking, and responsibility conditions. A mailing list, group participant, generic third party, class definition, or unrelated mention is insufficient. An exclusive employee-only permission contradicts; absence of either relation is NotMentioned.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"disclose to its representatives\",\"disclosed to its representatives\",\"disclose to agents\",\"disclosed to agents\",\"disclose to consultants\",\"disclosed to consultants\",\"furnish to representatives\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[\"representatives\"],\"any_phrases\":[\"need to know\",\"reasonably require access\",\"directly concerned\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"other than its employees\",\"anyone else except employees\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":false}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[377,416,487,238],\"rationale\":\"This rejects the observed false positive based on a participant mailing list while preserving operative permissions for professional and representative classes.\"},{\"operation\":\"UPDATE\",\"target_ids\":[\"nda-limited-use-evidence\"],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-limited-use-evidence\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-4\"],\"guidance\":{\"inspection\":\"Entail from an operative rule limiting use of protected information to the agreement's stated purpose or prohibiting every other use. Contradict when protected information or residuals may be used for broader internal-business or any purposes, even if disclosure remains restricted. A purpose-qualified copy, disclosure permission, ownership clause, or limited license does not itself decide use scope. Retain the operative use clause, object, purpose, exceptions, and polarity.\",\"source_queries\":[{\"all_phrases\":[\"use\"],\"any_phrases\":[\"only for\",\"solely for\",\"exclusively for\",\"except for\",\"other purpose\",\"own benefit\",\"purpose of this agreement\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[],\"any_phrases\":[\"internal business purposes\",\"own internal business purposes\",\"free to use for any purposes\",\"use for any purposes residuals\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true},{\"all_phrases\":[\"not use\"],\"any_phrases\":[\"confidential information\",\"evaluation material\",\"proprietary information\",\"confidential data\"],\"none_phrases\":[],\"include_list_preamble\":true}]}}, \"source_case_ids\":[377,487,245,490],\"rationale\":\"The draft treated broader internal-business use as support and a copying exception as a use limitation. The revised polarity test makes the observed contrast explicit.\"}],\"noop_reason\":null}"}}
